cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenRoboAssure, cite the v1.0.0 simulation benchmark package."
title: "OpenRoboAssure: A simulation-only reproducible assurance pipeline for physical-AI experiments"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/taechasith/OpenRoboAssure"
url: "https://github.com/taechasith/OpenRoboAssure/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
license: "Apache-2.0"
authors:
  - name: "OpenRoboAssure contributors"
abstract: >
  OpenRoboAssure is an open-source, simulation-only pipeline for reproducible
  physical-AI assurance experiments. The v1.0.0 package includes deterministic
  scenario generation, simulator adapters, policy benchmark artifacts,
  counterexample search evidence, coverage reports, hidden-target calibration
  evidence, and a clean software reproduction certificate. It does not establish
  physical-robot safety, learned-policy robustness, real-world reliability, or
  regulatory compliance.
